Third-party components
----------------------
This repository vendors one third-party project's source, EUC Thrills (below). Every other component is
fetched at build time from its registry or a pinned release and keeps its own license:

- Rust crates of the engine and CLI: see crates/THIRD_PARTY.md. All are permissive. deny.toml denies GPL
  everywhere except the optional development backend crates/euc-unicorn (Unicorn Engine, GPL-2.0), which is used
  only as a test oracle during development and is never part of a release build.
- MuJoCo 3.9.0 (Apache-2.0, Copyright DeepMind Technologies Limited), the physics engine, linked
  dynamically from the official release that tools/fetch-mujoco downloads and checks.
- Firmware: CMSIS 6 Core headers (Apache-2.0) and Unity (MIT), downloaded at configure time with pinned
  versions and sha256 checks; see firmware/README.md.
- EUC Studio app: npm packages and fonts, see app/THIRD_PARTY.md.

Outside EUC Thrills, one file adapts third-party source: firmware/core/math/libm.c derives its asin, atan and
atan2 from fdlibm, under this notice (kept in the file):

  Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved.
  Developed at SunPro, a Sun Microsystems, Inc. business.
  Permission to use, copy, modify, and distribute this software is freely granted, provided that this notice
  is preserved.

EUC Thrills
-----------
The rider figure of the app's 3D view is built with code from EUC Thrills by VibezZzCoder
(https://github.com/VibezZzCoder/EUC-thrills, commit a66dabd): its loft kit for lofted parts, its rider look
types, the rider's skeleton and arm-carriage values, and its rider construction with two-link IK. The copied
files are in app/src/vendor/euc-thrills (see its README.md); app/src/workspaces/ride/riderFigure/rig.ts adapts
the game's rider construction.

- Code: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 VibezZzCoder. The full text is in app/src/vendor/euc-thrills/LICENSE,
  and each copied or adapted file keeps the game's notice.

The look the figure wears, the street kit (app/src/workspaces/ride/riderFigure/streetKit.ts), is EUC Studio's
own. No asset of the game (its CC BY 4.0 geometry, colours or painted sheets) is part of EUC Studio. Earlier
versions used the game's fictional Cool Rider look under CC BY 4.0, with its attribution; it has been removed.
None of the game's riders is used.

Binary releases include the full license texts of everything they bundle.

